{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled","id":1450143,"title":"What are the Dream-souled?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-29T00:16:50-07:00","id":1450143,"title":"What are the Dream-souled?","content":"I've heard them mentioned, but does anyone have a place I can go and see what they are, exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T01:23:46-07:00","id":1450148,"title":"","content":"They're one of the 'optional canon' Exalted, slated to appear in an appendix to Exigents alongside the Hearteaters and Umbral Exalted (history, themes, example Charms).<br /> <br /> From what the writers have dropped, they're Chosen by a Wyld entity called Ketu, based on their potential to be a catalyst for recreating the world. Thing is, Ketu is a completely alien entity, all it knows of its candidates is their dreams, and all it knows of Creation is from the collective dreams of everyone in Creation. (Consider that in order to be capable of Exaltation by itself, Ketu must be a powerful and numinous being of Incarna level.)<br /> <br /> They're roughly Terrestrial-level, neutral with moonsilver and dissonant to everything else. Their animas are filled with images from their dreams.<br /> <br /> The two main themes of their Charmset are illusion and transformation, leaning towards messing with the perception/experience of reality. Charms include Rattling Toy Sabers, which lets them wield a broom like a goremaul, World-Mocking Evasion, which lets them reveal that what their enemy struck was only an illusion, and Right-Behind-You Terror, which makes their location ambiguous to people who can't see them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T20:43:59-07:00","id":1450267,"title":"","content":"Huh. Can you point me in the direction of a summary of the other two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T12:02:21-07:00","id":1450334,"title":"","content":"<b>Hearteaters</b>: Celestial-level. Resonant with adamant, neutral with the rest (a legacy of their original versions). Celestial Circle sorcery. They hunger to break wills and claim Pawns, even if they don't want to, courtesy of their manifestation of the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> By default, Pawns are human, though Hearteaters can expand their range. They don't have their minds eaten, they're imprisoned in themselves, aware of what's happening. Pawns can be freed externally or by the Hearteater themselves, although the latter's not necessarily a mercy.<br /> <br /> Their Incarna patron was killed during the Divine Revolution, his corpse used in a ritual to corrupt his Exalted into the Hearteaters. Following the Divine Revolution, the other Exalted drove them into the Wyld, slew them, and built well-warded prisons around the bones. Things being what they are, however, there's been a trickle of Hearteaters getting loose, which accelerated with the Usurpation, and then again with the Fair Folk invasion. Many have a grudge against the other Exalted due to their past life memories.<br /> <br /> While the Hearteaters are optional canon, their patron (and his death) is slated to be canonised in Exigents, his blood part of the Exaltation process of one of the example Exigents, the Sovereigns.<br /> <br /> When a Hearteater dies, the Exaltation will pass to a nearby Pawn with heroic potential and mental compatability with that Hearteater. If there's no Pawn nearby, it passes to whoever makes contact with the Hearteater's bones first.<br /> <br /> Hearteater combat: cruel, mind games, auroras that turn flesh to opal. Charmset concepts include direct control of Pawns, using their own Charms through them, and absorbing traits, abilities, and skills from them. Example Charm names include Pawn Becomes Queen, Empire-Self Expansion, Beautiful Monster Transformation, and Will-Crushing Victory Smirk.<br /> <br /> They can try bodyhopping, but the outcome can range from 'dominant personality in the new body' to 'thin smear of past life memories in the back of the new Hearteater's mind, if that'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Umbrals</b>: Celestial-level, (tentatively) resonant with soulsteel, neutral with everything else. Celestial Circle sorcery. Anima is shades of black and grey, with edges sometimes indigo, violet or scarlet. Gain power by giving into their Shadow, the manifestation of their darker side. Have a track to measure its influence on them, which increases when things are going horribly for them. They take it to fuel their Charms.<br /> <br /> Shadows aren't trying to get their Umbral killed, or necessarily trying to screw them over, but the Umbral may well not like how it goes about getting what it wants (think certain takes on the Hulk).<br /> <br /> Chosen from those with heroic potential and sufficient inner turmoil/self-doubt/self-hatred/etc. to form a Shadow when combined with a fragment of their patron's will and Essence. Patron was an Incarna who betrayed the others during the Divine Revolution, now imprisoned/deceased; the Umbrals were created after the Revolution. (Ambiguous exactly what their patron's status was when he created them.)<br /> <br /> Tend to amplify the dark sides of those around them, for better or worse. Charm concepts include manipulation of Shadows, shadows and darkness. Example Charm names include The Black Rose Blossoms, Elegant Monster Soliloquy, Fervid Nightmare Exploit, Preemptive Vengeance Declaration, and Your Worst Day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T14:17:17-07:00","id":1450354,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the summaries! I've apparently missed quite a bit since the last time I've checked those. Too bad that we are not going to get anything about the Spoken in the nearby future (unless I've also missed something about that as well)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T14:31:45-07:00","id":1450357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1450354#post1450354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the summaries! I've apparently missed quite a bit since the last time I've checked those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance got talkative on the unofficial Exalted Discord a while back, and had a session for each of the Optionals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T15:18:30-07:00","id":1450364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1450357#post1450357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vance got talkative on the unofficial Exalted Discord a while back, and had a session for each of the Optionals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for referring me to the Discord. I've just discovered that the patrons of the Getimians were spoiled and they are <i>freaking Oramus and Sacheverell</i>. Like, nope- didn't see THAT coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T15:37:07-07:00","id":1450367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dream-souled</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Hearteaters</b><br /> <br /> <b>Umbrals</b></span></span> </div> </div> </div>So, why are these 3 optional again? Did they have some sort of large enough setting impact the writers didn't want to have to write around their presence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T15:50:42-07:00","id":1450370,"title":"","content":"Well, I am not sure, but iirc there was somewhat of a controversy when they were introduced- some fans felt that there were too many new Exalts, and we didn't knew a lot about them during that time, and there was a worry about how heavily would the setting will be rewritten and how long people would have to wait for all Exalts to get their rulebooks and the bloated work overload and such and there was also the whole change in the dev team which took place, so due to either of those reasons, certain combination of those or some other reason entirely it was decided to turn them into &quot;optional&quot;. I assume that if they will be incredibly successful the devs may consider to fully &quot;canonize&quot; them to some degree, but that's the current situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T17:17:02-07:00","id":1450376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1450354#post1450354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the summaries! I've apparently missed quite a bit since the last time I've checked those. Too bad that we are not going to get anything about the Spoken in the nearby future (unless I've also missed something about that as well)</div> </div> </div> </div>For essence kickstarter there was a mention that they might be added in as a stretch goal in a a discord chat as many do have a desire to see them. <br /> <br /> Though as of posting this right now there is no such stretch goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T22:20:29-07:00","id":1450396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1450367#post1450367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, why are these 3 optional again? Did they have some sort of large enough setting impact the writers didn't want to have to write around their presence?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding was that, conceptually, they were liked, but, when it came time to try to build them out into full splats, they tended to just ...not have a lot to them and couldn't really be developed into something that felt like a full splat type.<br /> <br /> I think they could probably work fine as a single antagonist type or two, but they'd fit better under the Exigent Umbrella in that case too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T22:24:00-07:00","id":1450397,"title":"","content":"This post by Neall over at RPG.net kind of explains a bit of the logic for the Getimian patrons and in the process, at least one of the reasons for optionality.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/exalted-exalted-essence-merged.856038/post-23901519\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre.../post-23901519</a><br /> <br /> The big thing mostly is that there were already issues wiht making Exalts like Lunars fit in the setting as-was with how the setting was built and that was an issue for them for two editions prior, they just had a solution for...and were about to intrdouce at least two and as many as five new Exalts (not counting Exigents) that reintroduce teh whole effing problem in again. And that making them &quot;Just recently showe dup&quot; gets old when you have half the Exalts (Soalrs, Abyssals, infernals, Getimians, and more Exigents) being that already.<br /> <br /> And to introduce new beings fitting for new Exalts capable of Exalting whole new Hosts is hard to fit in a pretty full cosmology. ANd that it is also something htat isn't quite needed per se when you are alreay having in setting an &quot;All the rest' splat like Exigents. So with a lot of these issues, they kind of just fit being made Optional so that there were less expectaitons to make the setting account for them, and that it also let folks apply the aformentioend custom splat splat ot some stuff like that I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T23:35:17-07:00","id":1450402,"title":"","content":"How I think I\u2019m going to use the optional Exalted are as forces that arose and fell to help spice up certain stretches of the timeline, and possibly in historic campaigns. Like Heart-Eaters as a major Anathemae threat that the Dragon-Blooded Shogunate had to deal with in the mid reach of its reign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T03:05:51-07:00","id":1450426,"title":"","content":"Apparently Dream-souled are filling the niche of playable Fair Folk since that won't otherwise be a thing in this edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1450334#post1450334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the Hearteaters are optional canon, their patron (and his death) is slated to be canonised in Exigents, his blood part of the Exaltation process of one of the example Exigents, the Sovereigns.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't realize that. Is there anything we know about the Sovereigns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T03:26:28-07:00","id":1450433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1450426#post1450426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently Dream-souled are filling the niche of playable Fair Folk since that won't otherwise be a thing in this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by design - i.e., that wasn't why they were created - but that's how it's shaken out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't realize that. Is there anything we know about the Sovereigns? </div> </div> </div>Full name the Sovereigns of Uluiru, Terrestrial-level, resonant with adamant. To quote Vance's Discord posts:<br /> <br /> <i>They\u2019re members of a royal family in a Northwestern kingdom</i><i>, who descend into a subterranean cavern filled with a dead god\u2019s blood in hope of surviving and Exalting<br /> <br /> The Sovereign's deal is a bit weird. Cantata-of-the-Depths. the god who catalyzed the Exigence into the Sovereign's Exaltations, isn't the god whose blood fills that pool; he tapped into it to lend further power to his Exigents. The Sovereigns are one of those Exigents that blend the Essences of multiple deities, and have some backlash as a result.</i><br /> <br /> The key clue is from the Hearteaters' end; they have a particular interest in something in the city of Uluiru, suggesting that said dead god was their patron.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T10:46:38-07:00","id":1450468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1450402#post1450402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I think I\u2019m going to use the optional Exalted are as forces that arose and fell to help spice up certain stretches of the timeline, and possibly in historic campaigns. Like Heart-Eaters as a major Anathemae threat that the Dragon-Blooded Shogunate had to deal with in the mid reach of its reign.</div> </div> </div> </div>what I\u2019m leaning toward right now are Umbrals in the Late First-Age (though they may be tied to what is going on Gloam), Heart-Eaters in the mid-Shogunate, and Dream-Souled in the early Second Age while the post-apocalyptic world was recovering from the Great Contagion and Raksha invasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T13:49:28-07:00","id":1450496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1450334#post1450334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the Hearteaters are optional canon, their patron (and his death) is slated to be canonised in Exigents, his blood part of the Exaltation process of one of the example Exigents, the Sovereigns.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not quite right. The Sovereigns write-up does talk about the blood of an ancient god, but it provides no specifics. It's only in the Hearteaters section that we get details, and because the Hearteaters are optional, everything in their section (including the identity of their patron) is also optional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T15:09:12-07:00","id":1450510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1450334#post1450334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hearteaters</b>: Celestial-level. Resonant with adamant, neutral with the rest (a legacy of their original versions). Celestial Circle sorcery. They hunger to break wills and claim Pawns, even if they don't want to, courtesy of their manifestation of the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> By default, Pawns are human, though Hearteaters can expand their range. They don't have their minds eaten, they're imprisoned in themselves, aware of what's happening. Pawns can be freed externally or by the Hearteater themselves, although the latter's not necessarily a mercy.<br /> <br /> Their Incarna patron was killed during the Divine Revolution, his corpse used in a ritual to corrupt his Exalted into the Hearteaters. Following the Divine Revolution, the other Exalted drove them into the Wyld, slew them, and built well-warded prisons around the bones. Things being what they are, however, there's been a trickle of Hearteaters getting loose, which accelerated with the Usurpation, and then again with the Fair Folk invasion. Many have a grudge against the other Exalted due to their past life memories.<br /> <br /> While the Hearteaters are optional canon, their patron (and his death) is slated to be canonised in Exigents, his blood part of the Exaltation process of one of the example Exigents, the Sovereigns.<br /> <br /> When a Hearteater dies, the Exaltation will pass to a nearby Pawn with heroic potential and mental compatability with that Hearteater. If there's no Pawn nearby, it passes to whoever makes contact with the Hearteater's bones first.<br /> <br /> Hearteater combat: cruel, mind games, auroras that turn flesh to opal. Charmset concepts include direct control of Pawns, using their own Charms through them, and absorbing traits, abilities, and skills from them. Example Charm names include Pawn Becomes Queen, Empire-Self Expansion, Beautiful Monster Transformation, and Will-Crushing Victory Smirk.<br /> <br /> They can try bodyhopping, but the outcome can range from 'dominant personality in the new body' to 'thin smear of past life memories in the back of the new Hearteater's mind, if that'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Umbrals</b>: Celestial-level, (tentatively) resonant with soulsteel, neutral with everything else. Celestial Circle sorcery. Anima is shades of black and grey, with edges sometimes indigo, violet or scarlet. Gain power by giving into their Shadow, the manifestation of their darker side. Have a track to measure its influence on them, which increases when things are going horribly for them. They take it to fuel their Charms.<br /> <br /> Shadows aren't trying to get their Umbral killed, or necessarily trying to screw them over, but the Umbral may well not like how it goes about getting what it wants (think certain takes on the Hulk).<br /> <br /> Chosen from those with heroic potential and sufficient inner turmoil/self-doubt/self-hatred/etc. to form a Shadow when combined with a fragment of their patron's will and Essence. Patron was an Incarna who betrayed the others during the Divine Revolution, now imprisoned/deceased; the Umbrals were created after the Revolution. (Ambiguous exactly what their patron's status was when he created them.)<br /> <br /> Tend to amplify the dark sides of those around them, for better or worse. Charm concepts include manipulation of Shadows, shadows and darkness. Example Charm names include The Black Rose Blossoms, Elegant Monster Soliloquy, Fervid Nightmare Exploit, Preemptive Vengeance Declaration, and Your Worst Day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp. I definitely see the Black Lodge creature vibe in Hearteaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T15:43:35-07:00","id":1450514,"title":"","content":"I now wonder if the Sovereigns ends up being more similar to who the Hearteaters were more than the Hearteaters themselves.<br /> <br /> At any case, every new detail I learn about the Hearteasters makes me more excited to finally get them in Exigents. While they seem to definitely be on the &quot;villainous&quot; side, playing a Pawn-turned-Hearteater which has to struggle with their own corrupted Exaltation or try to utilize its monstrosity into heroic actions sounds like a cool concept for a character which I would like to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T02:08:12-07:00","id":1450553,"title":"","content":"Agreed; though while I've been excited for Heart-eaters for years, now the Umbrals sound really cool to me. Playing with a Shadow for a Hulk-like or even Venom-like experience was neat, but <i>literally</i> controlling shadows and darkness, and probably manipulating others' dark emotional urges as well, put me over the edge, along with their relationship with soulsteel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T11:05:09-07:00","id":1450610,"title":"","content":"You know, reading the Essence Alchemical preview made me wonder- in general the Alchemical's Caste somewhat corresponds to the themes of the Exalted with which its Magical Material resonates with- it is not a 1-to1 fit, there are some differences, but the general idea is more or less the same to some degree. Now, in Essence, the Adamant Caste is about serving as muses of their community who inspire and guide through social means and performances. The Hearteaters are all about emotional and mental manipulation, turning people into Pawns by &quot;playing their heartstrings&quot;. And we also know that the now dead patron of who the Hearteaters were would have been horrified to see their current state. I think that from here we can somewhat extrapolate that maybe before their fall from grace, the Hearteaters were the &quot;Artistic Exalted&quot;, who used some kind of ability to connect with the souls of others and guide them as muses- and then the Divine Revolution happened, the patron got themselves killed, and the former muses turned into sirens, turning their subtle guidance into a tyrannical horror, enforcing their own will instead of allowing others to bloom. <br /> <br /> By the same extrapolation the patron of the Umbrals may have to do something with punishment- or more exactly, self judgment/criticism. They did betrayed the rest of the Incrana, after all- maybe it was because they decided that the war caused more damage than it was worth, with the creation of the Neverborn and similar horrors, and their process of Exaltation is similar to forcing people to recognize and face with their own darkness as a form of &quot;catharsis&quot;. Maybe that was the goal in the case of the betrayal- the fallen Incrana wanted the rest of their kind to acknowledge and face the consequences of their own actions, or despised themselves for those act and wanted to &quot;cleanse&quot; themselves from those acts, and that led them to betray the gods in the war.<br /> <br /> Just some random theory, because I noticed that the Adamant Caste is somewhat different in presentation from its 2e form of being &quot;secret judges of the other Castes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T15:03:56-07:00","id":1450990,"title":"","content":"Big thanks to everyone out there who helps collect discord stuff and make it both more widely available and easier to come back and find later!<br /> <br /> Based on those writeups, I really want Umbrals in the game proper - those are really versatile themes with a cool aesthetic, and I'd probably have a lot more ideas for how to use them than Alchemicals or Liminals or whatnot.<br /> <br /> Hearteaters are also incredibly evocative, either as villains or antiheroes struggling to use their super evil powers in a good way, but sound pretty narrow. I think I'd be fine if there were 1-2 of them in the world (presumably, either due to their patron dying just as they were picking their first chosen, or due to said death causing all the exaltations to somehow collapse together). I want to use <i>a</i> Hearteater, but I'm not overwhelmed with thoughts of many of them, so I understand their optional status.<br /> <br /> Having a home for all the illusion and reality-warping Wyld stuff the Lunars never quite got is a cool goal, but even with this synopsis, I still feel like the Dream-Souled are too shrouded in mystery for me to get a feel for them. The most intriguing thing is probably the idea of a being understanding Creation in terms of its dreams rather than its reality, which is too bad, because that's the Patron's thing, not the PC's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T04:54:06-07:00","id":1451829,"title":"","content":"So for those who don't follow the Discord and weren't in the relevant stream, some new info about Hearteaters and Spoken-<br /> <br /> Hearteaters: their patron was Aurora, the Lord of Delight, and their original name was the Aurorals. They were shepherds and muses to the Exalted Host, and now they are... well, you know. The Sovereigns, who are their &quot;kin&quot; if you use that optional canon, have some kind of &quot;manifestation/gem&quot; mechanic, which makes me really think about Incarnum from D&amp;D 3e (or the metacreativity discipline)<br /> <br /> Spoken: their patron was Neptune, an Incrana who refused to take part in the Divine Revolution and was exiled to the West as a result. Eventually, the would be Spoken race found him (or he found them?), and they managed him to grant them Exaltation, yet either didn't knew or intentionally left out the price which was needed to be paid. The result was with the creation of the Spoken, and Neptune getting diminished into nothing about a Voice in the Trench.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T10:46:52-07:00","id":1451875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451829#post1451829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoken: their patron was Neptune, an Incrana who refused to take part in the Divine Revolution and was exiled to the West as a result. Eventually, the would be Spoken race found him (or he found them?), and they managed him to grant them Exaltation, yet either didn't knew or intentionally left out the price which was needed to be paid. The result was with the creation of the Spoken, and Neptune getting diminished into nothing about a Voice in the Trench.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they give any suggestion as to what Neptune was the Incarna of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26529-anshu","name":"Anshu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26529_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T12:44:49-07:00","id":1451895,"title":"","content":"Good time for info on the other Exalted, 'cause we got a loredump on the Umbral patron today in the Discord:<br /> <br /> He was the Incarna Nebiru, the Lord of Things Unseen, god of the invisible planet that bears his name. He refused to take part in the Divine Revolution out of fear of the Primordials' wrath.<br /> <br /> For his betrayal in the Revolution, he was imprisoned on his planet. Rather than suffer an eternity of imprisonment, he deliberately chose to die creating the Umbrals to free himself, his lingering echo in their Exaltations the seed crystal around which the Shadow forms<br /> <br /> His planet still exists, and is still invisible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T12:58:26-07:00","id":1451897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anshu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451875#post1451875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did they give any suggestion as to what Neptune was the Incarna of?</div> </div> </div> </div>They currently keep quiet on it even when asked directly about the subject","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T14:26:04-07:00","id":1451909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451897#post1451897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They currently keep quiet on it even when asked directly about the subject</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it's time to speculate! The name &quot;Neptune&quot; has oceanic associations, but tracing the lineage back through Classical Greek Poseidon to the Mycenaean deity there's also an association with earthquakes, and with their chosen being called &quot;the Spoken&quot; that suggests to me something perhaps related to thunder or other clamorous sounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26529-anshu","name":"Anshu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26529_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T15:46:33-07:00","id":1451917,"title":"","content":"Neptune being a earthquake god will make sense considering the Spoken's magical material which was now spoiled- Itzli/mirrorstone, a form of magical obsidian. Apparently it was hinted in Luthe's description as having obsidian spires and such.<br /> <br /> Also, Neptune seems to be somewhatb related to deep places in some way, but that's the most we got from pushing on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T16:03:56-07:00","id":1451921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451895#post1451895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good time for info on the other Exalted, 'cause we got a loredump on the Umbral patron today in the Discord:<br /> <br /> He was the Incarna Nebiru, the Lord of Things Unseen, god of the invisible planet that bears his name. He refused to take part in the Divine Revolution out of fear of the Primordials' wrath.<br /> <br /> For his betrayal in the Revolution, he was imprisoned on his planet. Rather than suffer an eternity of imprisonment, he deliberately chose to die creating the Umbrals to free himself, his lingering echo in their Exaltations the seed crystal around which the Shadow forms<br /> <br /> His planet still exists, and is still invisible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do have to say, now we know Nibiru's purview I have a much better time figuring out what shadows actually mean to Umbrals, in contrast to what shadows mean to Abyssals and to Infernals leaning on the Ebon Dragon. Things Unseen is a niche seperate from the Shadow of Death Abyssals have so I feel I have a better conceptualization now because of it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T00:54:36-07:00","id":1451960,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info on the optional Exalted, I'm really exited to learn more and I'm usually way out of the loop. Do we know anymore about the Architects? I remember them being name dropped a while ago but wasn't sure if we'd heard anything concrete about them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25202-dreamcaster","name":"Dreamcaster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T02:26:22-07:00","id":1451965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreamcaster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451960#post1451960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the info on the optional Exalted, I'm really exited to learn more and I'm usually way out of the loop. Do we know anymore about the Architects? I remember them being name dropped a while ago but wasn't sure if we'd heard anything concrete about them</div> </div> </div> </div>You have an Architect on page 552 of the Exalted 3rd Edition core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T02:48:04-07:00","id":1451966,"title":"","content":"And they'll be one of the example Exigents in the fatsplat (which'll have four full examples: Janest, the Architects, the Puppeteer, and the Sovereigns. Of the Puppeteer, all we know is 'Exalted by a spider puppet god').","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T04:12:31-07:00","id":1451974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451895#post1451895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good time for info on the other Exalted, 'cause we got a loredump on the Umbral patron today in the Discord:<br /> <br /> He was the Incarna Nebiru, the Lord of Things Unseen, god of the invisible planet that bears his name. He refused to take part in the Divine Revolution out of fear of the Primordials' wrath.<br /> <br /> For his betrayal in the Revolution, he was imprisoned on his planet. Rather than suffer an eternity of imprisonment, he deliberately chose to die creating the Umbrals to free himself, his lingering echo in their Exaltations the seed crystal around which the Shadow forms<br /> <br /> His planet still exists, and is still invisible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">icic, so they're the Chosen of Planet X, the forbidden Incarna those Sidereal plants in NASA don't want you to know about. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Jokes aside, I've really been looking forward to hearing more about the optional exalts, so thanks for sharing you guys.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","user":"TomDick&amp;Harry","date":". 06-13-2021, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","name":"TomDick&Harry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T22:06:10-07:00","id":1452112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451829#post1451829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoken: their patron was Neptune, an Incrana who refused to take part in the Divine Revolution and was exiled to the West as a result. Eventually, the would be Spoken race found him (or he found them?), and they managed him to grant them Exaltation, yet either didn't knew or intentionally left out the price which was needed to be paid. The result was with the creation of the Spoken, and Neptune getting diminished into nothing about a Voice in the Trench.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm surprised but pleased to hear teases about the Niobraran War exalts. Were these tidbit random or are we perhaps getting the Chosen of the Voice and the Chosen of the Depths in Exigents?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><a href=\"http://maidrpg.com\" target=\"_blank\">Maids</a> </span><span style=\"color:#404040\">+ Exalted = <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/maidzalt\" target=\"_blank\">Maid the RPG: Exalted Edition</a>! More chaos than you can shake an artifact feather duster at! Also, my <a href=\"https://www.obsidianportal.com/profile/Teleute\" target=\"_blank\">Obsidian Portal page</a>.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1853-teleute","name":"teleute","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1853_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T22:56:19-07:00","id":1452115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451895#post1451895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good time for info on the other Exalted, 'cause we got a loredump on the Umbral patron today in the Discord:<br /> <br /> He was the Incarna Nebiru, the Lord of Things Unseen, god of the invisible planet that bears his name. He refused to take part in the Divine Revolution out of fear of the Primordials' wrath.<br /> <br /> For his betrayal in the Revolution, he was imprisoned on his planet. Rather than suffer an eternity of imprisonment, he deliberately chose to die creating the Umbrals to free himself, his lingering echo in their Exaltations the seed crystal around which the Shadow forms<br /> <br /> His planet still exists, and is still invisible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remind me, do Umbrals resonate with Soulsteel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T23:05:50-07:00","id":1452116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>teleute</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452112#post1452112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm surprised but pleased to hear teases about the Niobraran War exalts. Were these tidbit random or are we perhaps getting the Chosen of the Voice and the Chosen of the Depths in Exigents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chosen of the Voice, aka Spoken: Not in the Exigent book itself, but no telling what stretchgoal s might contribute to a companion in the Kickstarter<br /> <br /> Chosen of the Depths: these were actually determined by the devs not to be a distinct Exalt type a while ago. It\u2019s just the collective term for the Dragon-Blooded, Exigents, Lunars, etc among the Pelagrothopes and aquatic Beastfolk on the Niobraran side of the war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T00:17:10-07:00","id":1452124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452115#post1452115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remind me, do Umbrals resonate with Soulsteel?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were at some point neutral to everything, but they fit souslteel well, and if you do include them and Hearteaters, hey, all six magical materials accounted for by Incarna-created Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 06-14-2021, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T00:22:50-07:00","id":1452125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452115#post1452115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me, do Umbrals resonate with Soulsteel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance tentatively decided they did, last it came up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452116#post1452116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chosen of the Voice, aka Spoken: Not in the Exigent book itself, but no telling what stretchgoal s might contribute to a companion in the Kickstarter</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall's comment on getting more on Neptune:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Neptune's tale will be told in the future, hopefully. <br /> <br /> For now, plz pledge to Exalted Kickstarts, k thx </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T06:12:42-07:00","id":1452152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451966#post1451966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of the Puppeteer, all we know is 'Exalted by a spider puppet god').</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen that Exigent type mentioned anywhere before. Where is that from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T06:21:26-07:00","id":1452153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452152#post1452152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen that Exigent type mentioned anywhere before. Where is that from?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have been mentioned a few times as the fourth Exigent type in the Exigents book, together with Janset, Sovereigns and Architects. Apparently a &quot;black market Exigent&quot;, I think her name is Pakpao. People always forget to ask about her compared to other Exalted types, leading to the fact we don't know much about her- &quot;which is how she likes it&quot;, as one of the devs said.<br /> <br /> EDIT-<br /> <br /> So I've collected some infor from the Discord- as it seems, the Puppeteer &quot;loves dragons&quot;, being her &quot;best taxidermy&quot;. She is the Chosen of the god of puppetry, and seems to lean more towards the mastermind/manipulator angle. Puppetry is their &quot;core gimmick&quot;, not sure how much is moving physical puppets or turn people/animals into puppets, but it is probably both. I actually don't find reference for any relation to spiders, but I see people talking about it in the Discord so maybe I just didn't dig deep enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 06-14-2021, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T06:45:04-07:00","id":1452158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452153#post1452153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don't find reference for any relation to spiders, but I see people talking about it in the Discord so maybe I just didn't dig deep enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Came up at the Exalted panel at the Onyx Path con, I think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T06:51:23-07:00","id":1452159,"title":"","content":"It seems very odd to me that Exigents will have notes in the appendices for creating Hearteaters, an Exalt type that the writers have shorthanded as being &quot;puppeteers&quot;<br /> more than once, and also full rules for an Exigent of a puppeteer god.<br /> <br /> That will probably make more sense when I can see them side-by-side, with all the subtle but meaningful differences. After all, Solars and Infernals both tend to be &quot;badass rebel&quot; types with Charms themed to vast sorcerous power, but I wouldn't mistake them for each other. Still, my first impression is bafflement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T06:55:07-07:00","id":1452160,"title":"","content":"It seems that Hearteater Pawns and Pakpao's Puppetry would have some fundamental differences- for example, I won't be surprised if the Puppeteer would be more focus on physical manipulation of puppets, while the Pawns are more through more of creating a &quot;soul hive&quot; around the Hearteater.<br /> <br /> Also, for those of you who had doubt, Exigence seems to physically come from a big fire which is found in Yu Shan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T07:53:01-07:00","id":1452163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452153#post1452153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have been mentioned a few times as the fourth Exigent type in the Exigents book, together with Janset, Sovereigns and Architects. Apparently a &amp;quot;black market Exigent&amp;quot;, I think her name is Pakpao. People always forget to ask about her compared to other Exalted types, leading to the fact we don't know much about her- &amp;quot;which is how she likes it&amp;quot;, as one of the devs said.<br /> <br /> EDIT-<br /> <br /> So I've collected some infor from the Discord- as it seems, the Puppeteer &amp;quot;loves dragons&amp;quot;, being her &amp;quot;best taxidermy&amp;quot;. She is the Chosen of the god of puppetry, and seems to lean more towards the mastermind/manipulator angle. Puppetry is their &amp;quot;core gimmick&amp;quot;, not sure how much is moving physical puppets or turn people/animals into puppets, but it is probably both. I actually don't find reference for any relation to spiders, but I see people talking about it in the Discord so maybe I just didn't dig deep enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's neat that she's been announced. I had a lot of fun writing for her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T08:43:38-07:00","id":1452171,"title":"","content":"I am hoping the Exigents companion book ends up containing some more of the name dropped Exigents like the Chosen of Masks, Dice, or Seals.<br /> <br /> If there\u2019s a reward tier to have a statted up starting Exigent (not a complete chat set, just what you need to get started or use them as a single npc) I\u2019m inclined to pitch a Chosen of the Guild jointly empowered by the Guild\u2019s major divine sponsors, with charms that literally work through the transition of abstract value to coinage and the exchange there of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T08:50:31-07:00","id":1452172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452171#post1452171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am hoping the Exigents companion book ends up containing some more of the name dropped Exigents like the Chosen of Masks, Dice, or Seals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will admit that little would make me happier than seeing a little expansion on the Bleak Warden. Definitely the most evocative of Exigent concepts to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T11:13:13-07:00","id":1452185,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m trying to get a grasp on what Aurora and Nibiru\u2019s divine domains would be distinct from those of Venus and Jupiter respectively","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T11:21:03-07:00","id":1452186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451895#post1451895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good time for info on the other Exalted, 'cause we got a loredump on the Umbral patron today in the Discord:<br /> <br /> He was the Incarna Nebiru, the Lord of Things Unseen, god of the invisible planet that bears his name. He refused to take part in the Divine Revolution out of fear of the Primordials' wrath.<br /> <br /> For his betrayal in the Revolution, he was imprisoned on his planet. Rather than suffer an eternity of imprisonment, he deliberately chose to die creating the Umbrals to free himself, his lingering echo in their Exaltations the seed crystal around which the Shadow forms<br /> <br /> His planet still exists, and is still invisible.</div> </div> </div> </div> So a while back, I was thinking about what celestial phenomenon might suit the Umbral's mysterious patron, and came up with &quot;the asteroid belt, I guess.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, it turns out that the guy who dreamed up the pseudoscientific Nibiru nonsense claimed that his imaginary, &quot;undiscovered&quot; planet created the asteroid belt by smashing into another planet.<br /> <br /> So... I was half right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T11:41:06-07:00","id":1452193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452185#post1452185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m trying to get a grasp on what Aurora and Nibiru\u2019s divine domains would be distinct from those of Venus and Jupiter respectively</div> </div> </div> </div>From what Elliot has said, I would look more into what jobs they were given by the Titans then just the concepts they would be in charge of. Venus and Jupiter are Gods of Love and Secrets respectively but in the context of the Loom of Fate and the creation of Destiny, helping administrating the duties of Creation's Gods who worked as slaves to the Makers of the Universe. Aurora if going by the songbird comparison, was likely in charge of handling the entertainment of the Primordials themselves. Them being the Lord of Delights likely in the context of managing all the things pleasurable for the mighty titans. That is how im looking at it. A very much a separation like how the Directional War Gods run their own division seperate from Mars, the Maiden of Battle. Despite them all being war gods with theoretically Mars on top but that is not the case.<br /> <br /> Edit: like looking at the description of the Aurorals. They were therapists and spiritual healers, this is a difference to the Chosen of Serenity who take a more larger picture approach of establishing peace","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 06-14-2021, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:04:22-07:00","id":1452209,"title":"","content":"Their context in their Exalt helps too. Aurora, Nebiru, and thier Chosen are like, alla bout that in all its forms and the drive. Venus and Jupiter are that <i>in context</i> <i>of Fate and Desitny</i>. That impacts their Exalts too.<br /> <br /> Kind of a weird thing to look at that 2e hinted at that 3e pushes more is that you can kinda see this in the different Alchemical Castes as prototypes of the other Exalted. In this context, you have Auroral Muses ala Adamant. Meanwhile, while Chosen of Serenity do do stuff wiht happense, joy, and love, it's notable that it's part of the kind of &quot;broad planning/management/big picture&quot; stuff of how it contributes to the other aspects. Similar wtih Nebiru versus Jupiter. Jupiter is about how secrets being hidden or revealed play in writing history. Nebiru is about like, secret police shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:45:14-07:00","id":1452222,"title":"","content":"Based on the Umbral Charm themes, Nebiru is also associated with shadows, darkness, and the Jungian shadow, which aren't major parts of Jupiter's associations; she's spying, stealth, wisdom and learning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T15:43:29-07:00","id":1452246,"title":"","content":"I don't really expect the writers to go here (not least because the Incarnae we're talking about are optional), but it's also worth noting that a lot of things were different before the Divine Revolution. Who's to say whether Venus was the Maiden of Serenity before Aurora died, or Nebiru was associated with secrets before being hidden away in darkness for all time?<br /> <br /> The Yozis are not the beings that existed before the War. A new realm was created, the nature of death itself scarred. Surely the primary duties of the Incarnae are not off the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T16:22:57-07:00","id":1452250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452171#post1452171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am hoping the Exigents companion book ends up containing some more of the name dropped Exigents like the Chosen of <b>Masks</b>, Dice, or Seals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at the very least it seems that the Onyx Path brochure has the art of the Chosen of Masks, so I am going to assume that we'll get something about her in Exigents, even if not a full writeup","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T06:46:01-07:00","id":1452465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451829#post1451829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">have some kind of &quot;manifestation/gem&quot; mechanic, which makes me really think about Incarnum from D&amp;D 3e (or the metacreativity discipline)</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything else on this? I don't have the Discord channel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T06:51:13-07:00","id":1452468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1452465#post1452465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything else on this? I don't have the Discord channel.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what one of the writers have said, Sovereigns have like gem constructs that answers to their every command as something they can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T14:54:11-07:00","id":1453596,"title":"","content":"I think one I'm hoping for now is a way for a Hearteater to 'purify' their exaltation, or for a genuine Auroral to be brought into the world as they were somehow. But that's probably along the lines of an Abyssal or Infernal being cleansed too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T15:00:39-07:00","id":1453600,"title":"","content":"Well, the devs has said before that they are not going to give us Auroral mechanics, so I assume that without having such there is no point in giving a way to purify the Hearteaters from their corruption. In should be noted that it was mentioned that the Hearteaters have interest with Uluiru, so maybe some of them believe that it could serve as a way to cleanse themselves in one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T17:54:16-07:00","id":1453614,"title":"","content":"Yeah, figured it wouldn't be an official thing. But really, trying to could be a great campaign goal!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T18:30:52-07:00","id":1453617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anshu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1451875#post1451875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they give any suggestion as to what Neptune was the Incarna of?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m gonna go out on a limb and guess \u201ca planet.\u201d <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T04:42:28-08:00","id":1501230,"title":"","content":"Given that the known details on the Hearteaters was that the Primordials did a horrific inversal ritual of sorts on Aurora's body, turning the Aurorals from therapists and muses into mind controlling 'celebrity' types. I feel like the idea of fixing that would be a whole Solar level campaign of sorts.<br /> <br /> It does make one wonder if there are other Celestial Incarna, even if dead, and what 'Inverted X Exalted' would be like...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6163-yama951","name":"Yama951","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T11:40:56-08:00","id":1501417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1453596#post1453596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one I'm hoping for now is a way for a Hearteater to 'purify' their exaltation, or for a genuine Auroral to be brought into the world as they were somehow. But that's probably along the lines of an Abyssal or Infernal being cleansed too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question indeed since while corrupted much like Abyssals or Infernals, what was done in turning Aurorals into Hearteaters could be considered more of a raw deal, more of a &quot;Great Curse plus&quot; in some ways than the making of a tool of the fallen Makers like those two groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1453600#post1453600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the devs has said before that they are not going to give us Auroral mechanics, so I assume that without having such there is no point in giving a way to purify the Hearteaters from their corruption. In should be noted that it was mentioned that the Hearteaters have interest with Uluiru, so maybe some of them believe that it could serve as a way to cleanse themselves in one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat shouldn't stop some creative folks there from extrapolating their own hypothetical Auroral charmset from &quot;mirroring&quot; Hearteater charms mixed in with some tinkering/guesswork from Adamant caste alchies tricks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And now veering with things in a quite different direction....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1450433#post1450433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Full name the Sovereigns of Uluiru, Terrestrial-level, resonant with adamant. To quote Vance's Discord posts:<br /> <br /> <i>They\u2019re members of a royal family in a Northwestern kingdom</i><i>, who descend into a subterranean cavern filled with a dead god\u2019s blood in hope of surviving and Exalting<br /> <br /> The Sovereign's deal is a bit weird. Cantata-of-the-Depths. the god who catalyzed the Exigence into the Sovereign's Exaltations, isn't the god whose blood fills that pool; he tapped into it to lend further power to his Exigents. The Sovereigns are one of those Exigents that blend the Essences of multiple deities, and have some backlash as a result.</i><br /> <br /> The key clue is from the Hearteaters' end; they have a particular interest in something in the city of Uluiru, suggesting that said dead god was their patron.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOk, maybe that's just my twisted mind playing tricks on me\u200b, but - northern kingdom whose subterranean depths hide caverns with the blood of a dead god/titan guarded by a host of supernatural beings empowered by it... anyone else gets a bit of Gethamane &amp; Vodak parallels from this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-26-2023, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T16:01:53-07:00","id":1505454,"title":"","content":"So apparently the Exigents backer pdf is out? Are the details about the apocryphal Exalted out yet?<br /> <br /> What are their castes/aspects? What martial arts and sorcery can they access? Are their Charms Ability-based, Attribute-based, or something else?<br /> <br /> Just what is a Shadow? And what is the deal with Ketu?<br /> <br /> Also are there any suggestions for when the apocryphals might have come into being (or been reawakened in the case of Hearteaters)? I was thinking it would make sense for Ketu to become interested in Creation when humanity survived the Balorian Crusade, and start gradually choosing Dream-Souled one at a time every few decades.<br /> <br /> Anything about how many of each apocryphal type there are? Do Umbrals and Hearteaters reincarnate in the same way as Celestial Exalted? Do Dream-Souled reincarnate or breed more of themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T16:56:09-07:00","id":1505457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505454#post1505454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently the Exigents backer pdf is out? Are the details about the apocryphal Exalted out yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire manuscript was given during the Kickstarter, as noted in another thread. This included the Appendix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505454#post1505454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are their castes/aspects? What martial arts and sorcery can they access? Are their Charms Ability-based, Attribute-based, or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're Essence-based for simplicity sake. They are not listed with Castes or Aspects since they're meant to be more design seeds. If someone would wish to expand on them, that's kind of for them and said as much in the text.<br /> <br /> Umbrals and Heart-Eaters can use up to Celestial Circle Sorcery and are &quot;netural' with Martial Arts (no Mastery, no Terrestrilal, don't learn SMA). Dream-Souled can learn Terrestrial CIrcle Sorcery and deal with the Terrestrial keyword with Martial Arts. Nothing is said on their access to necromancy.<br /> <br /> On Evocations: Hearteaters are Resonant with adamant and neutral with other materials, Umbrals Resonant with soulsteel and neutral with others, and Dream-Souled are neutral with moonsilver and Dissonant with other materials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505454#post1505454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just what is a Shadow? And what is the deal with Ketu?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow is how the Umbral Great Curse manfiests. It's basically a relfection of a character's negative emotions, doubts, anxieites, and so on manifested as a psychological construct that kind of wants to be in charge at expense of the Umbral Exalt. It is forged a bit from Nebiru's own hatred of the world and is kidn of fueld by the Incarna's remnants kind of super-charing their Great Curse in a way.<br /> <br /> Ketu is an unknown entity of notable power in the Wyld who only understands and interacts with Creation through dreams. That's about it. It's kind of mysterious by design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505454#post1505454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also are there any suggestions for when the apocryphals might have come into being (or been reawakened in the case of Hearteaters)? I was thinking it would make sense for Ketu to become interested in Creation when humanity survived the Balorian Crusade, and start gradually choosing Dream-Souled one at a time every few decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umbrals have always been there and are written as a rare-but-not-unheard of thing in Creation. Hearteaters were locked up for most of the First Age and started leaking out in the last few centuries. Dream-Souled it only says are kinda new, and not a lot is given on how new.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505454#post1505454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything about how many of each apocryphal type there are? Do Umbrals and Hearteaters reincarnate in the same way as Celestial Exalted? Do Dream-Souled reincarnate or breed more of themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's talked about in the text that it depends on the table, so numbers are given as ranges.<br /> <br /> Dream-Souled: 25-100<br /> Hearteaters: 200-400 Exaltations, 0-20 not locked-up.<br /> Umbrals: 50-200<br /> <br /> Dream-Souled Exaltations don't go to an inheritor. The Exaltation returns to Ketu, who incorperates it into what ever the hell Ketu does with it. So it generates them as-needed or has some process that sparks things like the Dragons I guess.<br /> <br /> Hearteaters incarnate in one of two fashions. First, if a suitable Pawn exists in range when she dies, her Exaltation moves there. It might, in fact, destroy the Pawn's personaltiy and just straight hijack the body, allowing the Hearteater to persist in some fashion. If no proper host is around, when she dies her bones turn into opals and if a mortal contacts them, the Exaltation transfers to them. Once again, depending on the strength of will, as well as time, since the last incarnation of the Exaltation, the Hearteater could supplant or supplement the new Exalt's personalty.<br /> <br /> Umbrals work more or less like other Celestial Exalted, since they well, are. Just generally going for folks with a lot of negative vibes to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T14:30:21-07:00","id":1505503,"title":"","content":"Thanks Blaque. It's really good to know the basics.<br /> <br /> I forgot to ask earlier: Are Hearteaters creatures of darkness?<br /> And do any of the new Exalted (incl. Getimians, Liminals, Architects, Sovereigns of Uluiru, new Infernals) have stated lifespans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T15:17:48-07:00","id":1505507,"title":"","content":"Architects don't live any longer than mortals, but cease to age so long as they're inside their city. Sovereigns can live for centuries but the full extent isn't known - Queen Ulu was around 320 before she got killed - and they show age sooner than other Exalts on account of being patchworks.<br /> <br /> Dream-Souled can live for a few centuries. Hearteaters are thought to live for at least a thousand years. Umbral lifespans are connected to how much of a hold their Shadow has over them - consistently higher Penumbra = a longer life\u200b\u200b.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","user":"TomDick&amp;Harry","date":". 03-16-2023, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","name":"TomDick&Harry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T20:24:53-07:00","id":1505524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505503#post1505503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot to ask earlier: Are Hearteaters creatures of darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think its ever stated, but probably, considering how they were all diced up by the other chosen for being monsters and had their remains imprisoned out in the Wyld. It could also be that this wasn't condoned by UCS, or whatever. Probably a table decision.<br /> <br /> Umbrals are definitely stated to be creatures of darkness, and Dream-Souled could be Enemies of Fate (given how much they screw up Destiny and how much they annoy Sidereals) but also might not be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T00:46:46-07:00","id":1505530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505524#post1505524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umbrals are definitely stated to be creatures of darkness, and Dream-Souled could be Enemies of Fate (given how much they screw up Destiny and how much they annoy Sidereals) but also might not be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the big factor in Dream-Souled being enemies of fate is that they're Exalted by a being from beyond Creation (which's how the Sids define Exalted enemies of fate, per Charting Fate's Course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T08:05:09-07:00","id":1505544,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> So I guess the Umbrals are creatures of darkness because their god was Forbidden. If that's so it implies the Spoken would also be creatures of darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T10:53:41-07:00","id":1505566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505544#post1505544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks.<br /> <br /> So I guess the Umbrals are creatures of darkness because their god was Forbidden. If that's so it implies the Spoken would also be creatures of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda. Nebiru was also like, <i>the god of darkness</i> back in the day too. I think regardless of his betrayal or not, his nature kind of just by definition makes Umbrals so. Neptune was banished more for neutrality not hostilty to my gathering. So the Voice of the Trench and its Chosen are kind of not subject to that since well, they were enemies fo the Chosen, not Heaven or the light.<br /> <br /> Kind of by all of this, this is probably while Heartaeaters aren't creatures of darkness. Aurora was dead and their Essences corrupted, but i'm pretty sure whatever makes osmething a creature of darkenss doesn't really apply to them. Theyw ere allies of the Exalted into the First Age. THey're just kind of horrific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T20:36:22-07:00","id":1505630,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the Apocryphal Exalted look a lot like different pieces of the Nocturnal fanslpat, (imprisioned traitor patron for Umbrals, Muses/Heralds for Aurals and too a lesser extent Dreamsouled) in that they touch on a lot of the same design space. Honestly, if Getimians were thrown in too...<br /> <br /> It does make the now long gone Aurals seem a lot more interesting though. Hearteaters aren't intended to be a playable splat though, as they very much are written as villains. Why yes, I'm still going ahead with my &quot;Doctor Who&quot; ripoff Hearteater. &quot;Fixing&quot; the condition is the goal (may need to find out about Sovreigns then steal away into the Lake), but maybe I should draw upon some more...Master-mind elements when the curse takes me.<br /> The fact that Regeneration/body theft is how Hearteaters &quot;exalt&quot; is diffinently an issue for entry. You are the bad guy, brainwashing and poessing people to survive.<br /> <br /> And yet Umbrals are the ones that play with &quot;you vs your darker self&quot; as a theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T00:10:21-07:00","id":1505644,"title":"","content":"I kind of find the irony to that actually part of the appeal. The Hearteater struggle is being a monster. The Umbral struggle has a notable bit where your Shaodw like, sin't suicidal or anything. It just hates you. So the conflict is quite different. But that the more monsterous of the two are the ones with the beautiful light themes is pretty neat, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T17:40:12-07:00","id":1505727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505630#post1505630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are the bad guy, brainwashing and poessing people to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's possible to approach such a subject with about as much nuance as the things that Lunars do to acquire human shapes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T19:32:04-07:00","id":1505744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505727#post1505727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's possible to approach such a subject with about as much nuance as the things that Lunars do to acquire human shapes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, it is possible. But there was a deliberate decision to NOT go that way. Which is fine, despite the Devs and RAW, there is no game police going to arrest my table because we try to make Hearteaters work as heroes, albeit tragic heroes. Their portrayal in the book makes it very clear we are meant to see them as villains, oir at least monsters.<br /> Other Exalts can do evil actions; heck splats like Abyssals and Infernals are built with that premise in mind. But there is no suggestion on how to do so for Hearteaters in a stable fashion. Which comes down to the flavour curse (with no mechanical weight atm) of needed to hollow out people and turn them, into Pawns.<br /> <br /> Just a reminder; I do want to play one. They are my favorite Exalt in Exigents, even over the cannical ones. But keep in mind their current design space puts them closer to BtP than I imagine most people would be comfortable with. The fact that this is a corruption from being the artistic muse/heralds/leaders that they were as Aurals plays well into the unintentional tragic monsters is a big hook, but EVERYONE sees them as monster. More so than any other group. <br /> They are Anathema that Lunars and Solars hunted from before the Usurpation, with good reason. They can only really be used in parties/circles that are entirely separated from this knowledge. Which means no Silver Pact or anyone who can call a Wild Hunt. Abyssals have more allies in the setting.<br /> <br /> Umbrals and Dreamsouled are far and away easier to integrate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T21:14:15-07:00","id":1505752,"title":"","content":"Something noted as missing in the current Appendix is actually the Great Curse of the different Apocryphals. I think that some more on the ways that the Curse manifests for them, notably for Dream-Souled and Hearteaters, I think can do a good job of solidfiying a bit of why they are at least perecieved how they are in setting.<br /> <br /> I think a thing to also note is a Lunar can opt-out of the face-taking. They can even find other ways to get shapes that aren't violent. Or use Charms that don't focus on shapeshifting much. But as a person on one of the Discord servers said, Hearteaters are kind of obligate Minonmancers. And when that is like, drawing on media exmaples like Kilgrave from <i>Jessica Jones</i> as a potential inspiration, you gotta have some pretty delicate hands on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T08:53:42-07:00","id":1505785,"title":"","content":"Can you please briefly summarize what the Great Curse is like for Dream-Souled? For that matter, why would they be Cursed since they definitely didn't exist during the Primordial War? It doesn't seem plausible to me for Dream-Souled or Liminals to actually have the Curse (vs. some other White Wolfy drawback).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-19-2023, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T16:33:26-07:00","id":1505839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505785#post1505785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you please briefly summarize what the Great Curse is like for Dream-Souled? For that matter, why would they be Cursed since they definitely didn't exist during the Primordial War? It doesn't seem plausible to me for Dream-Souled or Liminals to actually have the Curse (vs. some other White Wolfy drawback).</div> </div> </div> </div>We currently don't have Great Curse mechanics for the Apocryphal Exalts save teh intensity of an Umbral's Shadow Intimacy becoming stornger with more of their Limit-based trait. This is something that will be covered in the final version of <i>Out of the Ashes</i>.<br /> <br /> The Great Curse affects all Exalts in 3e, just differently. The Curse effects Exaltation itself, not the actual Exalted. This is mostly to make it so that there's not an out like 2e did with Abyssals, and also makes it so there isn't an attmept to make a different Bad Bar for every Exalt that's basically the Great Curse but not due to setting reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T17:36:50-07:00","id":1505852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505752#post1505752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think a thing to also note is a Lunar can opt-out of the face-taking. They can even find other ways to get shapes that aren't violent. Or use Charms that don't focus on shapeshifting much. But as a person on one of the Discord servers said, Hearteaters are kind of obligate Minonmancers. And when that is like, drawing on media exmaples like Kilgrave from <i>Jessica Jones</i> as a potential inspiration, you gotta have some pretty delicate hands on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, the backer-reward charm I requested for Many Faced Strangers explicitly requires <i>helping</i> people to gain their current form.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T09:20:04-07:00","id":1506145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505630#post1505630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the Apocryphal Exalted look a lot like different pieces of the Nocturnal fanslpat, (imprisioned traitor patron for Umbrals, Muses/Heralds for Aurals and too a lesser extent Dreamsouled) in that they touch on a lot of the same design space. Honestly, if Getimians were thrown in too...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's mostly because Nocturnals cast the net fairly wide following from the example set by MoEP: Lunars (and to a lesser extent Infernals) and as a result it's difficult to identify their important elements because different people have their own ideas about what parts of them were compelling or not. It's mostly a natural consequence of the difference between what 2e expected of a new exalt type vs. what Ex3 expects of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T12:17:49-07:00","id":1506161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1505839#post1505839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and also makes it so there isn't an attmept to make a different Bad Bar for every Exalt that's basically the Great Curse but not due to setting reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div> My personal hope is that Abyssal Limit still shakes out more like (1e) Resonance than the Limit mechanics of the 3e Exalted. Or, failing that, at least like the Doom of the Black Exaltation from <i>Shards.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T13:41:12-07:00","id":1506172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1450143-what-are-the-dream-souled?p=1506161#post1506161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My personal hope is that Abyssal Limit still shakes out more like (1e) Resonance than the Limit mechanics of the 3e Exalted. Or, failing that, at least like the Doom of the Black Exaltation from <i>Shards.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it can fork yeah. I think honestly I like how the current Celestial Limit works (for Solars, Lunars and Sidereals) where you have a list of fixed conditions, plus custom one, and how you break is reflective of the situation and your character.<br /> <br /> For Abyssals, something more like Doom I think fits. And I think there's still a want to hit something like the first scene in <i>Vampire Hunter D: Bloodlust</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}